1 NOTE Root place: Rasra, Ballia
1 NOTE Current place: Kanpur
1 NOTE Biographical Note Birthplace: Rasra, Ballia Education: BHMS, Allahabad University Life Summary Born in Rasra, Ballia, he pursued medical studies and completed his BHMS from Allahabad University, dedicating himself to a
2 CONC life of healing and service through homeopathy. He began his professional journey by establishing a homeopathy practice in his hometown of Rasra, quickly earning the trust and respect of the community for his heartfelt
2 CONC care and sincerity. On 5 November 1969, he married Firdaus Shahina, daughter of Advocate Rafique Ahmad Lari, in Lar—marking the beginning of a nurturing and dignified family life. In the early 1980s, he moved to Kanpur,
2 CONC where he co-founded Navratan Tannery in Jajmau (around 1979) with his brothers Maqbool and Akhtar. The name “Navratan” itself was a tribute inspired by his nine real brothers, symbolizing unity, strength, and the
2 CONC collective identity of the family. The tannery flourished for years and was eventually sold in the late 1990s to his brother-in-law, Ashfaque sb, closing a significant entrepreneurial chapter in the family’s journey. A
2 CONC long-term diabetic, he eventually succumbed to Chronic Kidney Disease (Stage 5) and passed away peacefully in June 2020 at the age of 78, leaving behind a legacy of humility, hard work, compassion, and quiet resilience.
