1 NOTE Suhail Zaheer Lari educated at Allahabad, Lahore, Karachi and Oxford. CEO and Director of various Public Limited companies. Author of An Illustrated History of Sindh, Neither Islamic Nor Persian, Meri Mitti key Log, Meri
2 CONC Society key Log, Makil under the Samma, Makli under the Mughals, Makli under Timurid, Makli under the Sufi. https://www.suhaillaripakistan.com Lari met his future wife Yasmeen Ahsan (later Yasmeen Lari) when he was in
2 CONC Lahore and she went on to study architecture in London. With their parents objecting to their marriage, he would write in his memoir that they threatened to get married in Scotland where the legal age for marriage was
2 CONC lower than that in England; their parents subsequently agreed to the union.[1] His wife, Yasmeen went on to become a prominent architect in Pakistan. The couple had two sons and a daughter.[1] Their house would be the
2 CONC site for artists, politicians, and writers to meet.[6] Lari died on 5 December 2020 from COVID-19 related complications. He was aged 84.[1][3]
